60: /**
61: * Computes the complex division.
62: *
63: * ## Notes
64: *
65: * -   See figure 10 of [reference][@baudin:2012].
66: *
67: * [@baudin:2012]: https://arxiv.org/abs/1210.4539
68: *
69: * @param re1      real component
70: * @param im1      imaginary component
71: * @param re2      real component
72: * @param im2      imaginary component
73: * @param re       real result
74: * @param im       imaginary result
75: */
